  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "claim_e155bdce3049462381f9ea2ff6e478b7",
      "statement": "The binary entrypoint cmd/step/main.go only injects build metadata and calls cmd.Run(): Version, BuildTime, and AppName are package variables set via -ldflags at build time (defaulting to \"N/A\" and empty), and package init() publishes them with step.Set, sets the CA client user agent to the version string, and applies the binary name via cmd.SetName.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://cmd/step/main.go#L10-L29",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:9d61d4a4bf529b8deb6e8682d4501b2fca8fe2213ebee5ea784d8dc6947d3b3a:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_47f9f6e3ece846758677fca31e92defd",
      "statement": "cmd.Run() wraps run() as os.Exit(run()), so the integer returned by run() is the process exit code; run() returns 0 on success and 1 when app.Run returns an error.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://internal/cmd/root.go#L46-L48",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:2226bf32d0ff614e4fe05cb898715b5f4994ecc66a3b7a13f59fd28fc8584e08:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_be052ef8a4f64ea1819031efcac23c28",
      "statement": "The boot sequence in run() is: defer panicHandler(), then step.Init() to initialize the cli-utils step environment (printing the error to stderr and exiting 1 if it fails), then app.Run(os.Args) on the app built by newApp. step.Init's implementation is owned by the external smallstep/cli-utils module (v0.12.2 in go.mod), not this repository.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://internal/cmd/root.go#L30-L44",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:f9fa64bb672657064979bc070b7384bed68f5506a51a855e664a942f483aa20e:"
